<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Malang is a city in the highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-java">East Java</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, and the second-largest city in the province. The area holds some of the earliest remains of Javanese kingdoms, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dinoyo-inscription">Dinoyo inscription</a> of 760 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/candi-badut">Candi Badut</a>, and later lay at the heart of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singhasari">Singhasari</a> kingdom. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> rule it became a cool hill town and plantation centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malang.jpg" alt="Malang" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Annisa Alwita from Malang, Indonesia · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tugu_Malang.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
